PRIORITY RULE :
*
+  - 
=

eg 1: a=5+2*4;  //2*4=8
     a=5+8;
     a=13;

When we have multiple operators within the same line which operator should be executed first will depends on the priority rule.
In the priority rule, Priority will decrease from top to bottom.

eg 2: a=5+2+4;   //5+4=7
      a=7+4;
       a=11;
When we have multiple operators which are belongs to same priority within the same line ,
in such scenario we need to depend on order of presidence rule
which tells us to execute the operators from "left" to "right"

eg 3: a=5*2+4;     a=5*(2+4);
      a=10+4;      a=5*6;
      a=14;        a=30;
Brackets are not having any priority just use it to change default priority order.

