Result sign depends on both numerator and denumerator . (normal mathmatical rules will be applied 
  eg : -5/2; //-2
        5/-2 ;  //-2
       -5/-2;     //2

If you want to eliminate units place digit from any number , that number should be divided with 10 ,
eg:   1234/10;  //123
      889/10;    //88

If the value of numerator is less than the denumerator the result will be zero.
eg:   10/20;    //0

Modulus Operator 
  Result of the modulus operator is reminder 
eg : 5%2;   //1
     10%5;   //0
     10%3;   //1

Result sign will depends on numerator sign as it is .
eg :   -5%2;    //-1
       5%-2;    //1
      -5%-2;     //-1

If the value of numerator is less then the denumerator the ans is numerator .
eg :    10%20;    //10
        100%300;    //100

If you want to extract only one unit place digit from any number , that number can be modulo with 10
eg :    1234%10;    //4

If we have x%y=10 then we ucan consider x is a multiple of y ,or y is a factor of x.
eg:    15%3;    //0

